The SDFGI investigation's logic
===============================

The action its story can run (`{run "jumpFlood"}`), stepping the jump flood's demonstration; the click handlers of
the probe maps' inset (`pickMapTexel`), the distance field's slice (`pickFieldCell`), and the byte chart
(`toggleByteRead`); and the click on the scene, which picks the light demonstration's floor cell.

$[Import* std]$[Import* render_lab_runtime]$[Import* godot_sdfgi_values]$[ImportAs rl_runtime rt]

The jump flood's last step (`floodStep`: the full-size pass).
$[# lastFloodStep 8]

The arguments a story passes to `jumpFlood` (`run.seconds=…`); the optional one is an option.
$[# JumpFlood [% {Struct {' {Field "seconds" Float} {Field "from" {Option Int}}}}]]

Steps the jump flood (`floodStep`) from `from` (the half-size seeds, 0, by default) to its full-size pass, one step
every `seconds`.
$[# jumpFlood {: {^ {elapsed run}
    [# seconds {.seconds run}]
    [# from {withDefault {.from run} 0}]
    {!if {<= seconds 0.0}
        {error f"{a step takes $seconds s; it takes longer than 0}"}
        {'
            {setFloodStep {float {min
                {+ from {steps seconds elapsed}}
                lastFloodStep}}}}}} {Action JumpFlood}}]

Picks the texel of the followed probe's maps under a click on their inset (`demos::maps_inset`): the two maps side
by side in a 408-pixel square, 24 pixels a texel, each 8 texels wide with its border, from row 108 down. A click on
a border texel or beside the maps picks nothing.
$[# pickMapTexel {: {^ {click}
    [# px {* {.u click} 408.0}]
    [# py {* {.v click} 408.0}]
    [# left {!if {< px 216.0} 0.0 216.0}]
    [# x {- {floor {/ {- px left} 24.0}} 1}]
    [# y {- {floor {/ {- py 108.0} 24.0}} 1}]
    {!if {< x 0}
        {'}
        {!if {< 5 x}
            {'}
            {!if {< y 0}
                {'}
                {!if {< 5 y} {'} {' {setMapTexel {float {+ {* y 6} x}}}}}}}}} ClickHandler}]

Picks the cell under a click on the distance field's slice inset (`demos::field_slices`): 34 cells of 0.2 m a side
from -3.4 m on x and z, rows from the top. The march, the readout, and the byte chart follow the picked cell.
$[# pickFieldCell {: {^ {click}
    [# col {clamp {floor {* {.u click} 34.0}} 0 33}]
    [# row {clamp {floor {* {.v click} 34.0}} 0 33}]
    {'
        {setFieldX {+ -3.4 {* {+ {float col} 0.5} 0.2}}}
        {setFieldZ {+ -3.4 {* {+ {float row} 0.5} 0.2}}}}} ClickHandler}]

A click on the byte chart switches its bars between the stored byte and the byte minus one, as a ray reads it.
$[# toggleByteRead {: {^ {click} {' {setByteRead {!if {< {byteRead} 0.5} 1.0 0.0}}}} ClickHandler}]

A click on the scene, in the light demonstration, picks the floor cell under it as the worked cell (`cellX`, `cellZ`):
its shadow ray, faces, and flags follow. Elsewhere, or on nothing, it picks nothing.
$[# scene {: {^ {click} {!if {= {demo} "light"}
    {caseOption
        {rt::trace {.u click} {.v click} {'}}
        {^ {} {'}}
        {^ {hit} {' {setCellX {.x {.point hit}}} {setCellZ {.z {.point hit}}}}}}
    {'}}} ClickHandler}]
